<!-- What changed in 2026 -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">What changed in 2026</span>
    <h2>The rules got tougher. Readiness is now year-round.</h2>
    <p class="lede">CMS finalized major changes to DMEPOS accreditation - and they raise the stakes for every supplier who bills Medicare.</p>
    <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top: 1.8rem;">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Annual reaccreditation</h3>
        <p>The old three-year cycle is gone. DMEPOS suppliers now face annual resurveys and reaccreditation - which means your policies, training logs, and site readiness have to hold up every single year, not once every three.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>New locations: survey first</h3>
        <p>As of January 1, 2026, a new location must be surveyed before it's accredited. The old three-month grace period to operate while waiting for a site visit no longer exists.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Ownership changes don't transfer</h3>
        <p>Accreditation does not automatically carry over after a merger, acquisition, or sale. Miss the required notifications to CMS and your accrediting organization, and billing privileges are at risk.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.8rem;">
      {%- if settings.calendly_url != blank -%}
        Not sure where you stand under the new rules? <a href="{{ settings.calendly_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Schedule a free readiness review →</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- How it works -->
<section class="section section--soft">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
    <h2>From first call to survey-ready binder</h2>
    <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top: 1.8rem;">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <h3>Schedule a readiness review</h3>
        <p>A free review of where your operation stands: your timeline, your risk areas, and which program fits - no pressure, no obligation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <h3>Complete your intake</h3>
        <p>A structured intake captures your products, staffing, and workflows so your program is written around reality, not boilerplate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <h3>Receive your program</h3>
        <p>Written, professionally printed, assembled, and shipped to your location - ready for the surveyor to open.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Featured products -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Programs</span>
    <h2>Built for where your operation is today</h2>

    {%- assign featured = collections[settings.featured_collection] -%}
    {%- if featured == blank or featured.products_count == 0 -%}
      {%- assign featured = collections.all -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top: 1.8rem;">
      {%- for product in featured.products limit: 6 -%}
        {% render 'product-card', product: product %}
      {%- else -%}
        <p>No products yet - add products in your Shopify admin and they'll appear here.</p>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top: 1.8rem;">
      <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">See all programs &amp; templates →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

